 "masterpiece": "after Leonardo da Vinci, Mona Lisa (c. 1503-19)",
 "artNote": "Title zone moved up from the judge's mid-height box (0.06 0.22 0.46 0.56) to the pale sky band (0.04 0.04 0.46 0.28), because the Creators opener sets its title near the top: the sky band is calmer (luma sd 14 vs 34) and reads better with dark ink (worst decile 8.9:1 vs 3.9:1). The mid-height valley still works if the title is set lower. Dark ink. Optional light ivory scrim (about 0.3, from the left edge to u 0.56) also softens what is left of the sky seam near u 0.50. Phone: dark ink in the sky, dek above v 0.21.",
